/users/Patashu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Patashu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-22T00:21:13Z","updated_at":"2025-01-22T00:26:32Z","body":"I am not sure this only happens on Firefox or that it's a new bug. I have a player of my Godot v3.53 game [Entwined Time](https://patashu.itch.io/entwined-time) who uses Chrome and occasionally reports the 'is the .pck file missing?' bug to me. At first I thought it only happened if I made multiple updates in quick succession and itch.io decided to return files from different versions so there was a mismatch, but even if I haven't made an update in over a week it will happen randomly some days. I'm not sure if itch.io, Godot or just the general concept of how browsers work is at fault. I think Ctrl+F5 fixes it but the end user shouldn't have to know to do this. (Also one of my users reports, on Firefox, they have to Ctrl+F5 THEN F5 to fix it. Dunno why.)\n\nMy .pck file is 67MB, if it matters. And for additional information, this is a game that tends to be played on a daily or weekly basis, so games that are only played once or infrequently might not demonstrate this bug as often.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2606011013/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"mini